tes the same tests as passing oracles.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6e3bf416563a6899","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope bullet 'Update only Stage-A tests and docs needed…' and Testing/AC lines citing test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py and test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory","norm_id":"n55fe7a0f36fbe30f","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author adds the scanner-integration job to gerrit-verify.yaml; the three existing not-in assertions fail; the cited oracle tests fail rather than pass as the AC claims."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Scope/Testing, list the exact assertions to invert: test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py (rewrite test_scanner_integration_runs_full_route_but_is_advisory + the `not in workflow[\"jobs\"]` line to assert the new advisory full-route job in gerrit-verify.yaml while still absent from vote.needs/normalization) and test_code_review_ws5.py::test_scanner_workflow_is_shared_by_mirror_and_gerrit_advisory (line 960).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that test_ci_workflow_parity.py must gain a NEW assertion for the full-route advisory scanner-integration job in gerrit-verify.yaml (it has none today), rather than describing it as an existing oracle.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search_files over tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py for 'scanner-integration' returned (no matches)","Plan AC: 'pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py proves gerrit-verify.yaml contains a full-route scanner-integration job using _scanner-integration.yml with Gerrit patchset inputs'"],"finding":"The plan presents test_ci_workflow_parity.py as an existing oracle proving gerrit-verify.yaml contains a full-route scanner-integration job, but that file has no scanner-integration coverage today; this is new test behavior (CREATION) that should be labeled as coverage to be added, not existing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6110082b78db5975","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing bullet and AC line 1 ('pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py proves gerrit-verify.yaml contains a full-route scanner-integration job')","norm_id":"n7ee77edf73ea5c33","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/author reads the AC as an existing oracle and runs the test unchanged, which passes vacuously without asserting the new job."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the auto-run scanner-integration job is excluded from the vote's WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION aggregation (im-open/workflow-conclusion snapshots ALL run jobs, not just vote.needs) so a scanner failure genuinely cannot cast Verified -1 in Stage A — omission from vote.needs and vote normalization alone is insufficient.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'do not add it to vote.needs, do not reference it in vote normalization' and AC: 'so it is advisory and cannot cast Verified -1'","gerrit-verify.yaml:504 CONCLUSION = `(<route checks>) && env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION || 'failure'`","gerrit-verify.yaml:438-441/464-469: WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION is a REST list-jobs snapshot of THIS RUN's jobs via im-open/workflow-conclusion — it aggregates job conclusions beyond vote.needs (that is precisely how optionality/artifact-probe get folded in)","A route='full' run with all explicit route jobs success but a failed scanner-integration would evaluate to `true && 'failure' || 'failure'` = 'failure' -> Verified -1"],"finding":"The plan's advisory-isolation mechanism (keep scanner-integration out of vote.needs and out of vote normalization) is incomplete: the vote's CONCLUSION expression folds in env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION, which im-open/workflow-conclusion derives from ALL jobs in the run, not just vote.needs. A failing auto-run scanner job would therefore turn WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION to 'failure' and cast Verified -1, contradicting AC #2 and recreating the anti-90c7 hazard Stage A is meant to avoid.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f92e56aad7e2d40cc","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope bullet 2 / Anti-90c7 safety design / AC line 2","norm_id":"n4e75a4742f9ad196","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A real full-route patchset whose diff trips a Semgrep/Gitleaks contract while every real gate passes","The very Stage-B patchset that introduces enforcement — a scanner failure there could already block via WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION even in Stage A"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Make the scanner job unable to redden the run-level conclusion, e.g. wrap its call so the reusable's job cannot report a failing conclusion in Stage A (continue-on-error at the caller, or have the Stage-A invoker consume the result without letting the job conclude 'failure'), and add a Stage-A test asserting that a simulated scanner-integration failure still yields vote-type='success' on a full route.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"system","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irr